# Shared SARA definitions

Use this unannotated module only for facts, types, and provision-neutral helper
computations shared by multiple statutory sections. Do not place a statutory
rule, required evaluator output, or cross-section API orchestration here.

Canonical input views: `parent_links` orients parent-child aliases;
`sibling_links` merges symmetric aliases; `date_of_birth` prefers an explicit
Birth fact and accepts relationship dates only when its fallback flag is true.
Birth dates and relationship-effective dates can legitimately differ (adoption).
Repeated event identities are deduplicated in event views, while gross income
counts consistent Income/Payment aliases once per transaction identity. Equal
amounts on different transaction identities remain distinct. Callers must use
input consistency validation before evaluation: gold `Api.TotalTaxFromWorld`
validates through `ValidatedWorld`; the raw API carries equivalent assertions.
The public World uses five lists. Legacy numbered slots are accepted only by
the Python migration adapter, which removes unused entries before conversion.

> Module Definitions

```catala-metadata
declaration enumeration TermKind:
  -- Atom
  -- String

declaration structure Entity:
  data id content integer
  data kind content TermKind

declaration enumeration KnownValue:
  -- AgriculturalLabor
  -- DomesticService
  -- Cash
  -- UnitedStates
  -- PrivateHome
  -- LocalCollegeClub
  -- CollegeFraternityOrSorority
  -- SicknessProvision
  -- AccidentDisabilityProvision
  -- DeathProvision
  -- EmployeeOrDependentProvision
  -- ReligiousOrganization
  -- Government
  -- Hospital
  -- EducationalInstitution
  -- Student
  -- ForeignGovernment
  -- StateGovernment
  -- OtherKnownValue

declaration enumeration FactValue:
  -- Known content KnownValue
  -- Named content Entity

declaration enumeration EventKind:
  -- Marriage
  -- Birth
  -- Death
  -- Income
  -- Payment
  -- Service
  -- Residence
  -- Migration
  -- Retirement
  -- Deduction
